      {w:"wise to",p:"adjective phrase",ipa:"/ˈwaɪz tə/",def:"(be wise to somebody/something) (informal) to know or understand about something, especially somebody's dishonest behaviour",tr:"…dan xabardor bo'lmoq / …ni tushunib qolmoq",ex:"Employers are now wise to the benefits of flexible workers."},
      {w:"bow",p:"noun",ipa:"/bəʊ/",def:"(another string to your bow) another skill or ability that you can use if the first one fails; a weapon for shooting arrows",tr:"kamon; (another string to your bow) yana bir mahorat/zaxira imkoniyat",ex:"Learning to code gives her another string to her bow."},
      {w:"ne",p:"abbreviation",ipa:"/ˌen ˈiː/",def:"(here: an unclear fragment from the episode, possibly part of a longer word or name) used here as in 'ne'er' (= never) in the phrase 'ne'er-do-well' (a lazy person who never achieves anything)",tr:"(bu yerda: noaniq bo'lak; ehtimol 'ne'er' – hech qachon)",ex:"A 'ne'er-do-well' is a lazy person — the opposite of a busy slasher."},
      {w:"popularise",p:"verb",ipa:"/ˈpɒpjələraɪz/",def:"to make a lot of people know about something and enjoy it",tr:"ommalashtirmoq",ex:"The term 'slasher' was popularised by a writer in the US."},
      {w:"dissatisfied",p:"adjective",ipa:"/dɪsˈsætɪsfaɪd/",def:"not happy or satisfied with something",tr:"norozi / qoniqmagan",ex:"Many people are dissatisfied with having only one job."},
      {w:"entrepreneurial",p:"adjective",ipa:"/ˌɒntrəprəˈnɜːriəl/",def:"having the qualities that are needed to succeed as an entrepreneur",tr:"tadbirkorlik qobiliyatiga ega",ex:"You need an entrepreneurial spirit to manage several careers."},
      {w:"balancing",p:"noun",ipa:"/ˈbælənsɪŋ/",def:"the act of giving the right amount of time and attention to different things; (balancing act) a process in which you try to please several people or do several things",tr:"muvozanatni saqlash",ex:"Having three jobs requires careful balancing."},
      {w:"peasant",p:"noun",ipa:"/ˈpeznt/",def:"(especially in the past) a person who owns or rents a small piece of land and grows crops, keeps animals, etc. on it",tr:"dehqon (kambag'al qishloq aholisi)",ex:"In the past, peasants often had several kinds of work."},
      {w:"bind",p:"noun",ipa:"/baɪnd/",def:"(informal) a difficult situation; (in a bind) in a difficult situation",tr:"(so'zl.) qiyin vaziyat / tang ahvol",ex:"If one job ends, you won't be in a bind because you have others."},
      {w:"once more",p:"adverb phrase",ipa:"/wʌns ˈmɔː(r)/",def:"one more time; again",tr:"yana bir marta / yana",ex:"Let me explain once more what a slasher is."}
